# hq — Server Environment Variables (dev)
# Copy to .env.server and fill in required values.
# Used by: wasp start (local development)

# ── Ports ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT=4101 — Wasp dev server port (avoids clash with default 3001 and other Wasp projects)
PORT=4101

# WASP_SERVER_URL — the URL HQ stores in SiteRegistry.siteUrl when this site
# connects. Mobile reads it from HQ to make brokered calls direct to this
# server, so it must be reachable from the device.
#   - Browser-only on the host:        http://localhost:4101
#   - Android emulator / LAN device:   http://<your-LAN-IP>:4101
# Localhost won't work from an Android emulator (localhost = the emulator).
#
# This single line is updated in place on every run of scripts/dev/start.sh
# (no flag → localhost; --lan → auto-detected LAN IP; --lan-ip <ip> → explicit).
# All other keys in .env.server are preserved.
WASP_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:4101

# ── Site Security ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no first-admin key to set: while hq has no users it prints a one-time
# link to set it up in its log at every start.

# SECRETS_MASTER_KEY — 32-byte base64 key for at-rest secret encryption: the
# GitHub App private key, every provider key (LLM and voice), and every stored
# model credential — a project's API key and a person's subscription login.
# REQUIRED: hq refuses to start without it. It also encrypts hq's own signing key,
# and every run needs a capability signed with that key. Losing or changing it
# makes anything already encrypted unreadable, so keep a copy.
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
SECRETS_MASTER_KEY=

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DATABASE_URL — only needed if NOT using wasp db start.
#                Format: postgresql://USER:PASS@HOST:PORT/DB
# DATABASE_URL=

# ── Filesystem ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# hq never reads or writes an Execution Site's disk: it names a location by its
# owner and asks the site that holds it, so SITE_ROOT is the site's setting alone
# (site/.env.server). Per-container settings (AGENT_CONTAINER_ISOLATION and
# AGENT_CONTAINER_MEMORY/PIDS_LIMIT/CPUS/ENDRUN_SECONDS/IDLE_MINUTES/
# PREFIX) are runtime-only too — set those on site, not here;
# site/.env.server.example documents each one.

# HQ_ASSETS_ROOT   — hq's own bundled assets (templates, library, presets). Optional:
#                    defaults to the assets directory beside the Wasp build (hq/assets locally,
#                    /app/assets in the image).

# HQ_STORAGE_ROOT  — hq's own storage: agent images, the voice cache, org board templates
#                    and library skills. REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION — the server refuses to
#                    start without it when NODE_ENV=production, because its fallback is
#                    the storage directory beside the Wasp build (/app/storage in the
#                    image), which does not survive an image upgrade. Optional locally,
#                    where that fallback is hq/storage and does survive.
#                    A site never reads it.

# ── Live preview (adr-0071) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PREVIEW_DOMAIN — a preview is served from a host name of its own, p-<id>.<this
#                  domain>, on hq's own port, never from hq's own address. Leave it
#                  unset in development: previews are then at
#                  http://p-<id>.preview.localhost:4101, which browsers resolve to
#                  this machine. A deployed hq (NODE_ENV=production) that sets none
#                  has previews off. See docs/architecture/deployment.md.
# PREVIEW_DOMAIN=preview.localhost

# ── Cross-origin (HQ brokered sessions) ───────────────────────────────────────
# HQ_ORIGIN — origin of the HQ app. Added to the site's CORS allow-list so HQ
#             browser sessions can call site Wasp operations and open WebSockets
#             cross-origin using a Bearer session token.
#             hq/client's Vite dev server runs on port 4110 (see hq/client/vite.config.ts).
HQ_ORIGIN=http://localhost:4110

# ── Dev login bypass (development only) ───────────────────────────────────────
# DEV_LOGIN_ENABLED  — when "true", `wasp db seed` creates a known ADMIN user so you
#                      always have a login after a database reset (no manual bootstrap).
#                      Set to "false" (or remove) to exercise the real bootstrap/invite
#                      sign-in flow instead. Never enable in production.
# DEV_LOGIN_USERNAME — username for the seeded dev user.
# DEV_LOGIN_PASSWORD — password for the seeded dev user.
DEV_LOGIN_ENABLED=true
DEV_LOGIN_USERNAME=dev
DEV_LOGIN_PASSWORD=devpassword
